      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "EL SALTO (1) is an old-timer lining up for start No 108, but is still racing in great heart, as evidenced by the last-start fourth at Echuca when beaten less than a length. Finished second the start prior, when beaten a length, and did start $2.20 that day. AMERICAN RUSS (5) beat home EL SALTO last start, albeit narrowly, but he does have just the one win from 49 starts, so he's hard to tip with confidence. Still, going too well to dismiss. FORTYFOUR MAGNUM (8) returned to the winner's stall last time at Kilmore in a stronger race than this, so he gores in everything despite the wide gate. THE MOUNT (3) resumes here and is yet to miss a place in three fresh runs and will have taken benefit from a recent Donald trial fourth placing. STEELY HUSTLER (11) is another who's drawn out, but made an encouraging return first-up and might have more improvement to come than most.",
